.TH AM5-SPD-DIAG 1 "2026-08-17" "am5-spd-diag 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
am5-spd-diag \- AM5 DDR5 SPD hub diagnostics after sleep / warm reboot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B am5-spd-diag
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Captures AMD AM5 DIMM/SPD identity across boot, shutdown, and systemd sleep/resume.
Detects firmware-visible SPD hub corruption (Unknown/missing part, 8-bit width,
SPD5118 MR11=0x08) after sleep and a warm reboot.
Sleep policy (deep / s2idle) is never changed.
.PP
Motherboard and DIMM serials are recorded for vendor tickets. System UUID and
asset tags are omitted.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Whether SPD identity is healthy right now.
.TP
.B analyze
Sleep/reboot history, corruption chain, hub evidence.
.TP
.B snapshot
Capture DIMM/SPD evidence now (polkit; snapshot helper only).
.TP
.B report
Polkit snapshot, then ticket markdown.
.TP
.B package
Polkit snapshot, then evidence tarball.
.TP
.B probe
Read SPD5118 MR11 on 0x50–0x53 (needs root; SMBus adapters only).
.TP
.B recover
Experimental in-band MR11 clear. Does not reboot.
.TP
.B purge
Delete captured logs. Does not uninstall the program.
.PP
A capture that finds current corruption posts a persistent urgent desktop
notification (no timeout). Clicking it opens a terminal on
.BR "am5-spd-diag status" .
Analyze and Report buttons run those commands. Acting on the notice
dismisses the banner but leaves it in notification history. GNOME can keep those
actions after the sender exits. Other common desktops (Plasma, XFCE,
Cinnamon, MATE, LXQt, dunst) only deliver clicks to the connection that
called Notify, so the sender stays connected until the notice is clicked
or dismissed. Report is paged with
.B glow
when available, otherwise
.B less .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/log/am5-spd-diag
Captures, reports, and packages.
.TP
.I /etc/am5-spd-diag.conf
Optional overrides.
.SH NOTES
From a source tree, polkit only elevates the installed helper
.I /usr/libexec/am5-spd-diag/pkexec-snapshot
\&. Install with
.B make PREFIX=/usr install
or a distro package. The internal
.B capture
subcommand is used by systemd units and is not listed in
.BR \-\-help .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmidecode (8)
